To read from a file, you can use the `fopen` function. This function takes two arguments: the name of the file and the mode in which you want to read from the file. The mode can be either `r` for reading or `w` for writing.

The following code shows how to read from a file:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>

#define FILENAME "data.csv"

int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    // open file for reading
    FILE *fp = fopen(FILENAME, "r");

    // read from file
    char *line = NULL;
    size_t len = 0;
    ssize_t read;
    while ((read = getline(&line, &len, fp))!= -1) {
        printf("%s\n", line);
    }

    // free memory
    free(line);

    return 0;
}
